{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D5","page":1,"quote":"10 (-0.05/-0.1)"},{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D6","page":1,"quote":"12 (-0.05/-0.1)"},{"kind":"note","ref":"N2","page":1,"quote":"# FINISH  :  I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"Dimensions D5 and D6 carry tight negative-only tolerances (-0.05/-0.1) on a part that will be zinc plated per note N2, but the drawing does not state whether these limits are before or after plating. Plating adds thickness that can push the finished diameters out of tolerance, causing assembly interference. The designer should specify if the toleranced sizes apply pre-plate or post-plate, or add an allowance for the coating thickness."

,"recommended_correction":"Add a note clarifying that dimensions D5 and D6 apply before plating (or adjust the limits to account for the specified I.Z.B.P. coating thickness)."},{"rule_id":"TL-002","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D5","page":1,"quote":"10 (-0.05/-0.1)"},{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D6","page":1,"quote":"12 (-0.05/-0.1)"}],"comment":"The two holes (features F1 and F2) carry only unilateral diameter tolerances with no fit designation, yet their tight negative-only tolerances suggest they are functional mating features. Without a stated fit class or explicit callout of the mating condition, manufacturing cannot verify the intended function and inspection lacks a clear acceptance criterion. The designer should add the appropriate fit designation or clarify the mating requirement for these holes."

,"recommended_correction":"Add a standard fit designation (e.g., H7/p6) or a note defining the mating condition for the holes dimensioned by D5 and D6."}]}
